  "content": {
    "id": "p58-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Let $C = 2x^{2} - 12x + 25$ represent the cost of manufacturing products in a day, where $x$ is the number of machines operating and $C(x)$ is in tens of thousands of dollars.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p58-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the cost of production if one machine is operating.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$150\\,000$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}C(1) &= 2(1)^2 - 12(1) + 25\\\\C(1) &= 15\\end{align*}$$\nThe cost is $15\\times\\$10\\,000=\\$150\\,000$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If the cost of production is $\\$90\\,000$, how many machines are operating?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "2 or 4 machines.",
          "worked": "Since $\\$90\\,000$ is 9 tens of thousands of dollars,\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2-12x+25 &= 9\\\\2x^2-12x+16 &= 0\\\\x^2-6x+8 &= 0\\\\(x-2)(x-4) &= 0\\\\x &= 2\\text{ or }4\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, 2 or 4 machines are operating.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find how many machines should be operated to minimise the cost of production and hence find the minimum cost of production.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "3 machines; minimum production cost $\\$70\\,000$.",
          "worked": "Since $a=2>0$, the vertex gives the minimum cost.\n$$\\begin{align*}x &= -\\frac{b}{2a}\\\\x &= -\\frac{-12}{2(2)}\\\\x &= 3\\\\C(3) &= 2(3)^2-12(3)+25\\\\C(3) &= 7\\end{align*}$$\nOperate 3 machines. The minimum cost is $7\\times\\$10\\,000=\\$70\\,000$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
